 "slug": "mellingen",
 "name": "Mellingen – Äbereich",
 "tagline": "Regenerative farm in the Reuss valley, Canton Aargau",
 "stage": "baseline",
 "stageNote": "Baseline in preparation. Nothing has been claimed or verified.",
 "summary": "An organic farm in Aargau's Reuss valley, close to floodplains of national importance, developed as a model for regenerative agriculture. NFA measures how ecological condition changes on the farm against independent reference areas.",
 "description": [
  "The Äbereich farm lies in the Reuss valley near Mellingen, close to floodplains of national importance. The farm stays in production. The project focuses on soil building, water retention, extensive grazing and agroforestry on permanently secured land.",
  "NFA designs the measurement, coordinates the partners, holds the evidence chain and publishes what can be published. The method adapts the open Wallacea Trust methodology to Swiss conditions: a field baseline, repeated measurements over time, independent review.",
  "Change on the farm is read against several lightly sampled reference areas, so the effect of the project can be separated from what happens in the wider landscape anyway."
 ],
